{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>עד עברי</b> Regarding Abraham it is written ויקרא בשם יהוה (Genesis 12:8), and it is human beings who are called to serve HaShem; therefore the word 'in the name of' is joined to the name of the One who is honored. It is not so with ויקרא בשם יהוה (below, 34:5), for there it is HaShem who calls; and likewise וקראתי בשם יהוה לפניך (above, chapter 19)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:40:06.258517758Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}